Rating guidelines: A company that designs exceptionally durable and safe products, provides fully transparent pricing with zero dark patterns or hidden fees, fully champions the Right to Repair with open documentation and affordable OEM parts, and honors warranties generously gets a 100. A company that complies with standard consumer protection laws, resolves complaints adequately, and avoids highly deceptive marketing gets a 50. A company that has repeated safety recalls, traps consumers with hidden recurring fees or dark patterns, exploits vulnerable populations with predatory pricing, or aggressively blocks independent repairs gets a 1.